!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = EpH4 mammary gland cell line
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: EpH4 mammary gland cell line stably expressing ES-FUCCI construct
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: NT
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = day postconfluency: 4
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = experimental repeat: 1
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = We transduced EpH4-FUCCI mammary epithelial cell line with non-targeted (NT), Traf3, or Traf3 plus p100 sgRNA lentiviruses. The cells were seeded at 100,000 cells/cm2 and cultured for 4 days, then trypsinized with 0.25% Trypsin (Gibco) and sorted on a FACSAria lll for mCherry+ (G1/G0) cells
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = EpH4-FUCCI cells were cultured in DMEM (Gibco) supplemented with 10% fetal bovine serum (Atlanta Biologicals), and 1x penicillin/streptomycin (Life Technologies).
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNeasy Mini Kit (Qiagen)
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNA libraries were prepared for sequencing using standard Illumina protocols
!Sample_data_processing = Sequenced reads were demultiplexed, trimmed for adaptor sequence, and masked for low-complexity or low-quality sequence using Illumina software
!Sample_data_processing = CLC Workbench was used for sequence mapping, data shown as reads per million mapped reads (RPM)
!Sample_data_processing = CLC Workbench was used to compare NT vs Traf3 KO and Traf3 KO vs Traf3/p100 double KO
